      "size": 10.981134414672852,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        128.69459533691406,
        527.4325561523438,
        143.13758850097656
      ],
      "text": "success versus all unfavourable outcomes. The evidence reviewers had planned to use two analytical",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.999899864196777,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        141.8946075439453,
        527.1948852539062,
        156.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "approaches designed to minimize bias; that is, marginal structural models to account for time-varying",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.974821090698242,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        155.09474182128906,
        527.58056640625,
        169.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "confounders, and for exact and propensity score matching of patient characteristics. However, sample",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.97692584991455,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        168.29469299316406,
        527.4486694335938,
        182.73768615722656
      ],
      "text": "size meant that there were limitations in how the first approach could be applied; also, owing to",
